Negative Numbers:
The number is stored into the memory into 2's complement beacuse it sets the msb(most significant bit to 1) depicting a negative number

Floating point numbers:
      memory respresentation: (1-bit sign)[-] (8-bit exponent)[--------] (23-bit mantisaa)[-----------------------]
      
1. Get the binary form of the given floating point number
2. Make the number in the form of (1.xx)*2^exp
3. Add bias to the exponent and get into binary form which will be the next exponent;
            (bias calculation => 2^(n-1)-1)
4. Number get converted back using the formula -> (-1)^sign * (1 + mantisaa) * 2^(exp-bias)

because of the truncation of the smaller precision value their value gets low;
